{"title":"Bayes' Theorem","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span id=\"Bayes.27_Theorem:\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Bayes'_Theorem:\">Bayes' Theorem:</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Bayes%27_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Bayes&#39; Theorem:\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/9/459b08d5235f417c69f0cc0c2d473a4739abdb1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/6/f263b4685391e1f4f3ba204a355cc203a29a0653.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> be two events, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/1/9d130e01eecca5b513cfbbacf4363867bb7d252d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(E_1 | E_2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"20\" /> the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Probability\" title=\"Probability\">probability</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/9/459b08d5235f417c69f0cc0c2d473a4739abdb1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> dependent on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/8/2e8a25c3a526fcb582fb6b04c918ed6d3d05decd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E_2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"17\" /> Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/8/8788a644959ccf9f27057cf0f963e442c51bf3ff.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P(E_1 | E_2) = \\dfrac{P(E_2 | E_1) \\cdot P(E_1)}{P(E_2)}.\\]\" width=\"244\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>~<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Enderramsby&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"User:Enderramsby (page does not exist)\">enderramsby</a>\n</p><p><br />\n<i>This article 